course: dictionary
lesson: 11402
title: Accomplish: succeeding after hard work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To accomplish something means to succeed in doing it, especially after hard work. Look for the clues: the work was hard, and the goal was reached. «Maya practised her spellings every night, and at last she accomplished her goal of reading a whole book.»
explain: Accomplish is a verb, so it changes its ending: accomplishes, accomplished, accomplishing. «The team accomplished the task before lunch.» Accomplished can also be an adjective, meaning very skilled. «She is an accomplished pianist» means she is very good at playing the piano.
explain: Context helps you again. In a school report, «What did you accomplish this term?» asks what you managed to do. To check your meaning, swap in a simpler word such as achieve or finish successfully. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Accomplish means to succeed in doing something, especially after hard work.
fact: «Mission accomplished» means the job is done.
fact: Accomplished as an adjective means very skilled, as in «an accomplished pianist».
fact: Accomplish is a verb: accomplishes, accomplished, accomplishing.
fact: Achieve is a close synonym, but accomplish often suggests that effort was needed to get there.
exercise: «After weeks of practice, Sam accomplished his goal of swimming two lengths.» What does accomplished mean here? | Gave up on it | Forgot all about it | Played it on the radio | *Succeeded in doing it
exercise: «She is an accomplished pianist.» What does accomplished mean? | Very tired | *Very skilled | Very late | Very loud
exercise: Which word means to succeed in doing something after hard work? | *Accomplish | Whisper | Forget | Wander
test: «Mission accomplished» means what? | *The job is done | The mission has just started | The mission was lost | Nobody knows the mission
test: «What did you accomplish this term?» asks what? | What you would like to eat | What the teacher wore | What you forgot to do | *What you managed to do
exam: Which sentence uses accomplished as an adjective? | They will accomplish it | *She is an accomplished swimmer | The team accomplished the task | We accomplish a lot each day
